# PAM's fallback for a service without a file of its own. PAM looks for it in
# this directory on every start (quickshell runs PAM with pam/ as its config
# directory); without it each lockscreen attempt logged "no default config
# other" as an error. Never used for anything real: everything is denied.
auth     required pam_deny.so
account  required pam_deny.so
password required pam_deny.so
session  required pam_deny.so
